Create a token and print ONLY the secret on stdout; details go to stderr. The
secret is shown once. It is for you, or with --agent for an agent you manage.
--expires-in takes a Go duration such as 720h (default from org settings);
an agent's token lives at most 1h, the default with --agent. --scope read
makes a token that cannot write.

Examples:
  export LORVIK_TOKEN=$(lorvik token create --name ci --expires-in 720h)
  lorvik token create --agent 106666050296328877

Usage
  lorvik token create [flags]

Flags
      --agent string        Mint the token for this agent id
      --expires-in string   Lifetime as a Go duration, e.g. 720h (default from org settings; 1h at most for --agent)
  -h, --help                help for create
      --name string         Label for the token
      --scope string        read or write (default write)

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)
